    "body": "@annevk made the changes you suggested.\r\n\r\nre: \"I don't really understand the need to change the ID and quotation marks.\"\r\n\r\nin the issue discussion Patrick had suggested an ID change to cut down on attributes with \"menu\" as the value.  I suppose having removed aria-haspopup from the example that is less of an issue now, but still seemed a change to help mitigate any further confusion.\r\n\r\nThe quote changes were because I was inconsistent with using single, double or no quotes, and noticed that the script example syntax highlighting wasn't working after the first line. I was hoping that changing the quotes to double quotes, aside from being more consistent with my other uses of quotes, would help fix that.",
